## SQ-TER-01 | terrain adaptation batch 4 load line
@group A
@commands boot; `grep '\[terrain-adaptation\] world load' latest.log`
@pass `trimmed` up by 4 (ponds x3, level-three ruins), `1 air-trimmed`, sunk starts up by 1 (carp pond); no warning naming a batch-4 id (ST-303)
@fails warning `sunk_start ... ignored`: the carp pond's start height is not a constant below 0 in this jar
@from batches/r1031/a1_boot.qb
bootexpect \[terrain-adaptation\] world load
bootreject \[terrain-adaptation\].*ignored
look the world-load line: trimmed up by 4, "1 air-trimmed", sunk starts up by 1 against the 2026-10-30 run (ST-303)

## SQ-TER-02 | ponds and the swamp fisherman house sit on a slope
@group A
@commands on a hillside: `/place structure farmers_structures:aquacultures_common`, `_carp`, `old_swamp_fisherman_house:fisherman_house`
@pass no square pad or air notch, the water stays in the pond, the rim flush with the slope; carp: no 4-block dip or plinth (ST-300)
@fails pond spills: water fill override `#water_fill/ponds`; plinth: `TerrainAdaptation#sink`
@from batches/r1031/w3_terrain.qb
@absent farmers_structures:aquacultures_common farmers_structures:aquacultures_carp (structure ids: listed in kubejs/exported/structures.json worldgen, not in the registry dump)
> execute unless entity qa run pbot spawn qa 0 150 0 minecraft:overworld creative
> execute positioned 2144 70 -2592 run locate biome minecraft:windswept_hills
waitlog nearest minecraft:windswept_hills is at 300
capture HL is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> tp qa {HL1} 200 {HL3}
sleep 25
> execute positioned {HL1} 120 {HL3} run place structure farmers_structures:aquacultures_common
> execute positioned {HL1+60} 120 {HL3} run place structure farmers_structures:aquacultures_carp
> execute positioned {HL1-60} 120 {HL3} run place structure old_swamp_fisherman_house:fisherman_house
reject (?i)failed to place|unknown structure
look positions {HL1},{HL3} / +60 / -60: no square pad or air notch, water stays in the pond, rim flush with the slope; carp: no 4-block dip or plinth (ST-300)

