## SQ-TER-06 | ocean geodes covered in the floor block (floorPatch SWAP)
@phase long
@group B
@commands Chunky r 300 over deep ocean; `/locate feature` is not available, so fly the floor (spectator) over 5 geode spots (`/locate biome minecraft:deep_ocean`, look for calcite / basalt)
@pass `SWAP` (default): no basalt or calcite showing; geodes that reach the floor are mounds of the floor's own sand / gravel, amethyst only in the opening; then set `floorPatch = "CUT"`, restart, a fresh square: geodes cut flush, rim in the floor block; prismarine geodes (Geode Plus) untouched in both (ST-305)
@fails basalt still showing: `floorPatch` OFF or the RETURN injector failed (mixin error in latest.log); air pocket under water: `patchColumn` water rule
@from batches/r1031/w3_terrain.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> execute positioned 0 70 0 run locate biome minecraft:deep_ocean
waitlog nearest minecraft:deep_ocean is at 300
capture GO is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> chunky center {GO1} {GO3}
> chunky radius 300
> chunky start
waitlog Task finished 1800
> forceload add {GO1-64} {GO3-64} {GO1+63} {GO3+63}
sleep 20
# 128 x 128 sample at the square centre in four 64 x 44 x 64 tiles (the box limit is 262144 blocks)
> cdevtest count {GO1-64} 20 {GO3-64} {GO1-1} 63 {GO3-1} minecraft:calcite
> cdevtest count {GO1} 20 {GO3-64} {GO1+63} 63 {GO3-1} minecraft:calcite
> cdevtest count {GO1-64} 20 {GO3} {GO1-1} 63 {GO3+63} minecraft:calcite
> cdevtest count {GO1} 20 {GO3} {GO1+63} 63 {GO3+63} minecraft:calcite
> cdevtest count {GO1-64} 20 {GO3-64} {GO1-1} 63 {GO3-1} minecraft:smooth_basalt
> cdevtest count {GO1} 20 {GO3-64} {GO1+63} 63 {GO3-1} minecraft:smooth_basalt
> cdevtest count {GO1-64} 20 {GO3} {GO1-1} 63 {GO3+63} minecraft:smooth_basalt
> cdevtest count {GO1} 20 {GO3} {GO1+63} 63 {GO3+63} minecraft:smooth_basalt
> cdevtest count {GO1-64} 20 {GO3-64} {GO1-1} 63 {GO3-1} minecraft:amethyst_block
> cdevtest count {GO1} 20 {GO3-64} {GO1+63} 63 {GO3-1} minecraft:amethyst_block
> cdevtest count {GO1-64} 20 {GO3} {GO1-1} 63 {GO3+63} minecraft:amethyst_block
> cdevtest count {GO1} 20 {GO3} {GO1+63} 63 {GO3+63} minecraft:amethyst_block
> forceload remove {GO1-64} {GO3-64} {GO1+63} {GO3+63}
reject verb=\S+ .*done=0
look the verb=count lines give n and on= (what each stands on); calcite and smooth basalt seen from the water (first block below water) should be about 0: fly 5 geode spots in the client block for the look (ST-305); prismarine geodes untouched. count reads loaded chunks only (skipped_columns 0 means the sample was loaded) Chunky while they are still loaded, else forceload the box first

## SQ-TER-07 | ported structure datapacks stay in terrain_adaptation/soft and template_trim; absent-mods list drops them
@phase worldgen
@group A
@commands boot; `/cdevtest tag structure creativeworldgen:terrain_adaptation/soft` and `creativeworldgen:template_trim`; `grep "\[absent mods\]" logs/kubejs/server.log`
@pass both tags list `forest_ruins:ruin_1` (with the other ported datapacks: illager_siege_weapons, eugene, ...); no `[absent mods]` line names forest_ruins or illager_siege_weapons (r1118 F1: about 520 entries dropped as absent mods)
@fails tag helper `_ents` dropped them: `global.has.datapack` false (Creative Common `DataNamespaces` empty: `ReloadableServerResourcesMixin` missed, or the namespace is not in the reload's resource manager)
@jars creativecommon creativeworldgen creativedevtools
@from plan_bugfix_r1118.md B2
@absent creativeworldgen:template_trim (a structure tag, not a registry id)
> cdevtest tag structure creativeworldgen:terrain_adaptation/soft
expect verb=tag kind=structure tag=creativeworldgen:terrain_adaptation/soft n=[1-9]\d* ids=\S*forest_ruins:ruin_1
> cdevtest tag structure creativeworldgen:template_trim
expect verb=tag kind=structure tag=creativeworldgen:template_trim n=[1-9]\d* ids=\S*forest_ruins:ruin_1
shell grep -h "\[absent mods\]" logs/kubejs/server.log | grep -E "forest_ruins|illager_siege_weapons|eugene" | cut -c1-200; true
shell test "$(grep -h "\[absent mods\]" logs/kubejs/server.log | grep -cE "absent (forest_ruins|illager_siege_weapons|eugene)$")" = 0
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
look both tags hold the ported structures; the absent-mods lines name only real absent mods

